update content_bodies set title = '大垣まつり（R4.5.15）', description = '大垣まつりは、美濃地方を代表する祭礼行事であり、大垣の城下町で伝承されてきました。この祭りは、大垣藩主から下賜された軕と町衆の軕が共存する形態が全国的にも珍しく、からくり人形や軕上の芸能には中京圏や近畿圏の影響が見られ、東西の祭礼文化の交渉を示しています。これは国内の山・鉾・屋台行事の伝播や変遷を理解する上で重要な役割を果たしています。大垣市は岐阜県の西部に位置し、豊富な地下水に恵まれた「水の都」として知られています。また、松尾芭蕉の紀行文「奥の細道」のむすびの地であり、関ケ原合戦の際には西軍の本拠地となった大垣城や、豊臣秀吉が一夜で築いた墨俣一夜城などの歴史的な名所もあります。3月下旬から5月には舟下りやたらい舟、大垣まつりが開催され、多くの観光客で賑わいます。' where id = 'fERHFXQ1OGgqvXgylI1Qi';
update content_bodies set title = 'Ogaki Festival (R4.5.15)', description = 'The Ogaki Festival is a traditional event representing the Mino region, celebrated in the castle town of Ogaki. It features a unique coexistence of floats granted by the Ogaki feudal lord and those from the townspeople, making it a rare occurrence nationwide. The festival''s karakuri puppets show influences from the Chukyo region''s float events, while the performing arts on the floats reflect the traditions of the Kinki region, highlighting the cultural exchange between eastern and western Japan. This festival is significant for understanding the transmission and evolution of float events across the country. Ogaki, located in Gifu Prefecture, is known for its abundant underground water and historical sites, including Ogaki Castle and the Sumiyoshi Castle, which was built overnight by Toyotomi Hideyoshi. The city hosts various attractions and events, including boat rides and the UNESCO-listed Ogaki Festival, attracting many tourists from late March to May.' where id = 'L6X4s_jyqAUiU_z1B2Fft';
